# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository.
# Without this, committing from Windows ships CRLF into Linux containers,
# which breaks shell scripts and Docker entrypoints at runtime.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that run inside containers must always be LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never diff or convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated — collapse in PR diffs.
#
# `merge=binary` is the important one. A lockfile is machine-written JSON with
# thousands of near-identical blocks, so git's line merge will happily splice
# two versions together and produce a file that is no longer valid JSON — which
# is exactly what happened when the dependabot upgrades were merged, breaking
# `npm ci` for every branch until it was regenerated. Marking it binary makes
# git stop and report a conflict instead; the resolution is always to take one
# side and re-run `npm install`, never to merge by hand.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff merge=binary
